    "title": "Lesson 02: Anatomy of an HTML Document: DOCTYPE, html, head, and body",
    "slug": "html-lesson-02-anatomy-of-an-html-document-doctype-html-head-and-body",
    "category": "programming",
    "track": "html",
    "track_name": "HTML5 Track",
    "category_name": "HTML5 Fundamentals",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Understand the strict structural requirements of a modern HTML5 document.",
    "content": "# Lesson 02: Anatomy of an HTML Document: DOCTYPE, html, head, and body\n\nEvery HTML page follows the same basic skeleton. Once you know it by heart, you can start any web page in seconds.\n\n## 1. The skeleton\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Page title</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <h1>Visible content goes here</h1>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\n## 2. Each part explained\n\n| Part | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `<!DOCTYPE html>` | Tells the browser \"this is modern HTML5\". Must be the very first line. |\n| `<html lang=\"en\">` | The root element containing everything. `lang` helps screen readers, translation and search engines. |\n| `<head>` | Information **about** the page - title, character set, CSS links. Not shown on the page. |\n| `<body>` | Everything the visitor **sees**: text, images, buttons. |\n\nThink of it like a letter: the `<head>` is the envelope (address, stamp), the `<body>` is the letter itself.\n\n## 3. The document tree\nHTML elements form a **tree** - parents, children and siblings:\n```text\nhtml\n├── head\n│   ├── meta\n│   └── title\n└── body\n    ├── h1\n    └── p\n```\n`head` and `body` are **siblings** and both are **children** of `html`. This tree is called the **DOM** - JavaScript will use it later.\n\n## 4. Worked examples\n### Example 1: An Arabic page\nFor right-to-left languages, set `lang` and `dir`:\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <title>مرحبا</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>مرحبا بكم في مدرسة برقيسي</h1>\n  <p>هذه صفحة باللغة العربية تُقرأ من اليمين إلى اليسار.</p>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n### Example 2: Comments\nComments are notes for developers; the browser ignores them:\n```html\n<!-- Main header starts here -->\n<h1>Monthly Report</h1>\n<!-- TODO: add the sales chart below -->\n<p>Sales grew 12% this month.</p>\n```\n\n### Example 3: Indentation makes structure visible\nBrowsers ignore extra spaces, but humans don't. Indent children by 2 spaces:\n```html\n<body>\n  <div>\n    <h2>Products</h2>\n    <p>Eye drops and gels.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n```\n\n### Example 4: Whitespace collapses\nMultiple spaces and line breaks in HTML become **one space** on screen:\n```html\n<p>Sales      were\n   very         good.</p>\n```\nRenders as: *Sales were very good.* Use `<br>` for a line break or separate `<p>` elements.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> In VS Code type `!` then press **Tab** - it writes the whole skeleton for you.\n\n## 5. Common mistakes\n- **Content inside `<head>`**: a `<p>` in the head is moved or ignored.\n- **Missing DOCTYPE**: the browser switches to old \"quirks mode\" and layouts behave strangely.\n- **Two `<body>` tags** - a page has exactly one head and one body.\n\n## 6. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Write a complete skeleton with `lang=\"en\"`, charset, viewport and the title \"Weekly Report\".\n2. In the body add a heading, two paragraphs, and an HTML comment explaining each section.\n3. Draw (as a comment) the document tree of your page.\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Weekly Report</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- Page heading -->\n  <h1>Weekly Report - Week 46</h1>\n\n  <!-- Summary paragraph -->\n  <p>Total sales reached 48,000 SAR this week.</p>\n\n  <!-- Next steps paragraph -->\n  <p>Next week we focus on the Makkah region.</p>\n\n  <!--\n  html\n  ├── head (meta, meta, title)\n  └── body (h1, p, p)\n  -->\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- Every page: DOCTYPE, html, head, body.\n- `head` = information about the page; `body` = visible content.\n- HTML forms a tree of parent, child and sibling elements.\n",
