    "title": "Lesson 05: Text Semantics: strong, em, mark, small, blockquote, code, and pre",
    "slug": "html-lesson-05-text-semantics-strong-em-mark-small-blockquote-code-and-pre",
    "category": "programming",
    "track": "html",
    "track_name": "HTML5 Track",
    "category_name": "HTML5 Fundamentals",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Highlight and format text meaningfully using modern semantic HTML elements.",
    "content": "# Lesson 05: Text Semantics: strong, em, mark, small, blockquote, code, and pre\n\nHTML has many small elements that give text **meaning** - importance, emphasis, code, quotations. Using the right one helps screen readers, search engines and your CSS.\n\n## 1. Importance and emphasis\n\n| Element | Meaning | Default look |\n|---|---|---|\n| `<strong>` | Strong importance, warning | **bold** |\n| `<em>` | Stress emphasis (changes meaning when read aloud) | *italic* |\n| `<b>` | Bold for style only (keywords, product names) | **bold** |\n| `<i>` | Alternate voice: technical terms, foreign words | *italic* |\n| `<mark>` | Highlighted / relevant text | yellow background |\n| `<small>` | Side comments, fine print | smaller text |\n\n```html\n<p><strong>Warning:</strong> do not touch the tip of the bottle.</p>\n<p>I <em>never</em> said she stole the money.</p>\n```\n\n## 2. Quotations\n```html\n<blockquote cite=\"https://www.who.int\">\n  <p>Health is a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>As the saying goes, <q>prevention is better than cure</q>.</p>\n```\n- `<blockquote>` - a long, separate quotation (indented block).\n- `<q>` - a short inline quotation (browser adds quote marks).\n- `<cite>` - the title of a work: `<cite>The Lancet</cite>`.\n\n## 3. Code and preformatted text\n```html\n<p>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>S</kbd> to save.</p>\n<p>Use the <code>SUM()</code> function in Excel.</p>\n<pre>\nName      Sales\nAhmed     14,000\nSara       9,000\n</pre>\n```\n- `<code>` - a piece of code.\n- `<kbd>` - keyboard input.\n- `<pre>` - preformatted: keeps spaces and line breaks exactly.\n\n## 4. More useful inline elements\n```html\n<p>H<sub>2</sub>O and E = mc<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>Price: <del>120 SAR</del> <ins>95 SAR</ins></p>\n<p><abbr title=\"World Health Organization\">WHO</abbr> guidelines</p>\n<p>Meeting on <time datetime=\"2026-11-20\">20 November</time></p>\n```\n\n## 5. Worked examples\n### Example 1: A product notice\n```html\n<h2>Eye Drops 10ml</h2>\n<p><mark>New formula</mark> - now preservative-free.</p>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> discard 28 days after opening.</p>\n<p><small>Prices include 15% VAT.</small></p>\n```\n\n### Example 2: A tutorial snippet\n```html\n<p>To create a total, type <code>=SUM(B2:B10)</code> and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>.</p>\n<pre><code>=IF(C2&gt;=10000, \"Target met\", \"Below target\")</code></pre>\n```\nNote: inside HTML, write `<` as `&lt;` and `>` as `&gt;` when you want them shown as text.\n\n### Example 3: HTML entities\n\n| Write | Shows |\n|---|---|\n| `&lt;` `&gt;` | < > |\n| `&amp;` | & |\n| `&nbsp;` | non-breaking space |\n| `&copy;` | © |\n| `&quot;` | \" |\n\n```html\n<p>&copy; 2026 Bargisy eSchool &amp; Partners. Use &lt;p&gt; for paragraphs.</p>\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Choose elements by **meaning**, then style with CSS. `strong` tells a screen reader \"this is important\" - `b` and a CSS class do not.\n\n## 6. Common mistakes\n- **Using `<pre>` for layout** - it's for code and fixed-format text only.\n- **Writing `<` directly in text** - the browser may read it as a tag; use `&lt;`.\n- **Using `<blockquote>` just to indent** - use CSS margin.\n\n## 7. Hands-on Student Challenge\nCreate a \"Promotion\" card containing:\n1. A highlighted word \"Limited offer\".\n2. An old price crossed out and a new price.\n3. A strong warning about the expiry date with a `<time>` element.\n4. The keyboard shortcut Ctrl + P to print the coupon.\n5. Fine print about VAT and a copyright line using entities.\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<h2>Promotion</h2>\n<p><mark>Limited offer</mark> on Hydrating Eye Gel</p>\n<p>Price: <del>85 SAR</del> <ins>65 SAR</ins></p>\n<p><strong>Valid until <time datetime=\"2026-11-30\">30 November 2026</time> only.</strong></p>\n<p>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>P</kbd> to print this coupon.</p>\n<p><small>Prices include 15% VAT. &copy; 2026 Al Shifa Pharmacy &amp; Partners.</small></p>\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- strong/em carry meaning; b/i are stylistic.\n- blockquote, q and cite for quotations; code, kbd and pre for technical text.\n- Use entities like `&lt;` `&amp;` `&copy;` to display special characters.\n",
    "tags": "HTML, Front-End, Lesson 05, Web Development",
    "read_time": 4,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
