    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Target elements based on their exact relationships in the DOM hierarchy.",
    "content": "# Lesson 04: Combinators: Descendant, Child (>), Adjacent (+), and General Sibling (~)\n\n**Combinators** select elements based on their **relationship** to other elements - inside, directly inside, or next to.\n\n## 1. The four combinators\n\n| Combinator | Syntax | Selects |\n|---|---|---|\n| Descendant | `A B` (space) | Every B anywhere inside A |\n| Child | `A > B` | B that is a **direct** child of A |\n| Adjacent sibling | `A + B` | The B **immediately after** A (same parent) |\n| General sibling | `A ~ B` | **Every** B after A (same parent) |\n\n## 2. Descendant vs child\n```html\n<style>\n  .menu a { color: #2563eb; }        /* all links inside .menu */\n  .menu > li { border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; }   /* only top-level li */\n</style>\n<ul class=\"menu\">\n  <li><a href=\"#\">Products</a>\n    <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"#\">Eye care</a></li>   <!-- link is blue, li has NO border -->\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li><a href=\"#\">Contact</a></li>\n</ul>\n```\n\n## 3. Sibling combinators\n```html\n<style>\n  h2 + p { font-weight: bold; color: #0f766e; }   /* first paragraph after each h2 */\n  h2 ~ p { margin-left: 16px; }                   /* every paragraph after the h2 */\n</style>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>Lead paragraph - bold and indented.</p>\n<p>Second paragraph - indented only.</p>\n<p>Third paragraph - indented only.</p>\n```\n\n## 4. Worked examples\n### Example 1: Styling an article\n```html\n<style>\n  article { font-family: system-ui; max-width: 480px; }\n  article h2 + p { font-size: 18px; color: #334155; }   /* intro paragraph */\n  article p a { color: #ea580c; }                        /* links in paragraphs */\n  article > footer { color: #94a3b8; font-size: 13px; }\n</style>\n<article>\n  <h2>Blink more at your screen</h2>\n  <p>We blink up to 60% less when looking at screens.</p>\n  <p>Read the <a href=\"#\">full guide</a> for more tips.</p>\n  <footer>Posted on 15 Nov 2026</footer>\n</article>\n```\n\n### Example 2: Spacing between items with `+`\nThe \"lobotomized owl\" style - add space only **between** items:\n```html\n<style>\n  .stack > * + * { margin-top: 12px; }\n  .stack > * { margin: 0; background: #e0f2fe; padding: 8px; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"stack\">\n  <p>First</p>\n  <p>Second</p>\n  <p>Third</p>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Example 3: A checkbox controlling a sibling (no JavaScript)\n```html\n<style>\n  .details { display: none; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 8px; }\n  #show:checked ~ .details { display: block; }\n</style>\n<input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"show\"> <label for=\"show\">Show details</label>\n<div class=\"details\">Delivery within 24 hours in Jeddah.</div>\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Keep selectors short. `.card-title` is easier to read and override than `body main section .cards div > h3`.\n\n## 5. Common mistakes\n- **Thinking `+` / `~` look backwards** - they only select elements that come **after**.\n- **Siblings must share the same parent.**\n- **Long descendant chains** that break when HTML changes.\n\n## 6. Hands-on Student Challenge\n```html\n<div class=\"faq\">\n  <h3>Delivery time?</h3>\n  <p>24 hours in Jeddah.</p>\n  <p>48 hours in other cities.</p>\n  <h3>Returns?</h3>\n  <p>Within 14 days.</p>\n  <div class=\"note\"><p>Nested note paragraph.</p></div>\n</div>\n```\n1. Make the paragraph directly after each h3 bold.\n2. Give every **direct** child paragraph of `.faq` a left padding of 12px (the nested note paragraph must not get it).\n3. Make all paragraphs anywhere in `.faq` grey.\n4. Make every `.note` that comes after an h3 have a yellow background.\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<style>\n  .faq h3 + p { font-weight: bold; }\n  .faq > p { padding-left: 12px; }\n  .faq p { color: #64748b; }\n  .faq h3 ~ .note { background: #fef9c3; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"faq\">\n  <h3>Delivery time?</h3>\n  <p>24 hours in Jeddah.</p>\n  <p>48 hours in other cities.</p>\n  <h3>Returns?</h3>\n  <p>Within 14 days.</p>\n  <div class=\"note\"><p>Nested note paragraph.</p></div>\n</div>\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- Space = descendant, `>` = direct child, `+` = next sibling, `~` = all following siblings.\n- Sibling combinators only look forward and need the same parent.\n- Prefer short, class-based selectors.\n",
