    "id": "css-44",
    "lesson_number": 44,
    "title": "Lesson 44: Modern Centering: 3 Ways to Center Anything in CSS",
    "slug": "css-lesson-44-modern-centering-3-ways-to-center-anything-in-css",
    "category": "programming",
    "track": "css",
    "track_name": "CSS3 Track",
    "category_name": "Modern CSS & Design",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Review margin: auto, absolute centering with transform, and Flexbox centering.",
    "content": "# Lesson 44: Modern Centering: 3 Ways to Center Anything in CSS\n\n\"How do I centre a div?\" is the most famous CSS question. Today there are simple, reliable answers for every case.\n\n## 1. Choosing a method\n\n| What to centre | Method |\n|---|---|\n| Inline text / inline elements horizontally | `text-align: center` on the parent |\n| A block with a width horizontally | `margin: 0 auto` |\n| Anything both ways | Grid: `display: grid; place-items: center` |\n| Anything both ways (flex) | `display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center` |\n| An overlay / popup on top of other content | `position: absolute; inset: 0; margin: auto` or `top:50%; left:50%; transform: translate(-50%,-50%)` |\n\n## 2. Worked examples\n### Method 1: Grid - the shortest\n```html\n<style>\n  .box { display: grid; place-items: center; height: 180px; background: #e0f2fe; border-radius: 12px; font-family: system-ui; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"box\"><div>Perfectly centred with 2 lines of CSS</div></div>\n```\n\n### Method 2: Flexbox\n```html\n<style>\n  .box { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 10px; height: 180px; background: #fef3c7; border-radius: 12px; font-family: system-ui; }\n  .box span { background: white; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 8px; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"box\"><span>One</span><span>Two</span><span>Three</span></div>\n```\nFlex is best when centring a **row** of items.\n\n### Method 3: Absolute + transform\n```html\n<style>\n  .stage { position: relative; height: 180px; background: #ede9fe; border-radius: 12px; }\n  .popup { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);\n           background: white; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 10px; font-family: system-ui; box-shadow: 0 8px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.15); }\n</style>\n<div class=\"stage\"><div class=\"popup\">Centred overlay</div></div>\n```\n`top/left: 50%` moves the top-left corner to the centre; `translate(-50%, -50%)` shifts back by half the element's own size.\n\n### Method 4: margin auto for horizontal centring\n```html\n<style>\n  .page { max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 16px; font-family: system-ui; }\n  .page h1 { text-align: center; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"page\"><h1>Centred page</h1><p>The container is centred with margin auto; the heading text with text-align.</p></div>\n```\n\n### Example 5: Centring a full-screen login card\n```html\n<style>\n  body { margin: 0; }\n  .screen { min-height: 100vh; display: grid; place-items: center; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a, #1e3a8a); font-family: system-ui; }\n  .login { width: min(90%, 340px); background: white; padding: 24px; border-radius: 16px; }\n  .login input { width: 100%; padding: 10px; margin: 6px 0 12px; box-sizing: border-box; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"screen\">\n  <form class=\"login\"><h2>Sign in</h2><input placeholder=\"Email\"><input type=\"password\" placeholder=\"Password\"><button>Log in</button></form>\n</div>\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Default to **grid + place-items: center** for single items and **flex** for rows of items. Both work even when you don't know the element's size.\n\n## 3. Common mistakes\n- **Vertical centring with no height** on the parent - there's no space to centre within.\n- **`margin: auto` without a width.**\n- **`text-align: center` on a block child** - it centres the text inside, not the block itself.\n\n## 4. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Centre a 120px circle avatar inside a 250px-tall card using grid.\n2. Centre a row of three buttons horizontally and vertically in a 100px-tall toolbar using flex.\n3. Centre a \"Loading...\" badge over an image using absolute + transform.\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<style>\n  body { font-family: system-ui; }\n  .card { display: grid; place-items: center; height: 250px; background: #f1f5f9; border-radius: 14px; }\n  .avatar { width: 120px; height: 120px; border-radius: 50%; background: #0f766e; color: white; display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 2rem; }\n  .toolbar { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 10px; height: 100px; background: #e2e8f0; margin: 12px 0; border-radius: 10px; }\n  .image { position: relative; width: 300px; height: 180px; background: url(\"https://picsum.photos/id/1021/600/360\") center / cover; border-radius: 12px; }\n  .loading { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); background: rgba(0,0,0,.7); color: white; padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 999px; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"avatar\">MA</div></div>\n<div class=\"toolbar\"><button>Day</button><button>Week</button><button>Month</button></div>\n<div class=\"image\"><span class=\"loading\">Loading...</span></div>\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- text-align: center for inline content; margin: 0 auto for blocks with a width.\n- grid + place-items: center is the simplest way to centre in both directions.\n- absolute + translate(-50%, -50%) centres overlays.\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 44, Web Design, Beginner",
