    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "summary": "Deep dive into modern Flexbox layout architecture: mastering flex sizing part 1: understanding flex-grow (distributing extra space).",
    "content": "# Lesson 52: Flex Sizing Part 1: Understanding flex-grow (Distributing Extra Space)\n\n`flex-grow` decides how flex items **share extra space** in the container. It's a ratio: an item with `flex-grow: 2` gets twice as much **extra** space as one with `flex-grow: 1`.\n\n## 1. How it works\n1. The browser lays out items at their base size.\n2. It calculates the **leftover space**.\n3. It shares that leftover space according to the grow values.\n\n```css\n.item { flex-grow: 0; }   /* default: don't grow */\n.item { flex-grow: 1; }   /* take a share of extra space */\n```\n\n## 2. Worked examples\n### Example 1: One item grows\n```html\n<style>\n  .row { display: flex; gap: 6px; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 6px; font: 13px system-ui; margin-bottom: 8px; }\n  .row div { background: #3b82f6; color: white; padding: 10px; border-radius: 6px; }\n  .grow { flex-grow: 1; background: #16a34a !important; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"row\"><div>Logo</div><div class=\"grow\">Search box takes all remaining space</div><div>Cart</div></div>\n```\n\n### Example 2: Ratios\n```html\n<style>\n  .r { display: flex; gap: 6px; font: 13px system-ui; }\n  .r div { padding: 10px; color: white; border-radius: 6px; flex-basis: 0; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"r\">\n  <div style=\"flex-grow: 1; background:#0ea5e9\">1</div>\n  <div style=\"flex-grow: 2; background:#6366f1\">2</div>\n  <div style=\"flex-grow: 1; background:#0ea5e9\">1</div>\n</div>\n```\nWith `flex-basis: 0`, all space is \"extra\", so widths become exactly 25% / 50% / 25%.\n\n### Example 3: Search bar layout\n```html\n<style>\n  .search { display: flex; gap: 8px; width: 100%; max-width: 480px; font-family: system-ui; }\n  .search select { padding: 8px; }\n  .search input { flex-grow: 1; padding: 8px 10px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; }\n  .search button { padding: 8px 14px; }\n</style>\n<form class=\"search\">\n  <select><option>All</option><option>Eye care</option></select>\n  <input placeholder=\"Search products...\">\n  <button>Search</button>\n</form>\n```\n\n### Example 4: Sidebar + content\n```html\n<style>\n  .layout { display: flex; gap: 12px; height: 160px; font-family: system-ui; }\n  .side { width: 180px; background: #0f172a; color: white; padding: 10px; border-radius: 10px; }\n  .main { flex-grow: 1; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding: 10px; border-radius: 10px; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"layout\"><aside class=\"side\">Fixed 180px sidebar</aside><main class=\"main\">Content grows to fill the rest</main></div>\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> flex-grow distributes **leftover** space, not total width. If items have different content sizes, `flex-grow: 1` on all of them won't make them equal - add `flex-basis: 0` (or use `flex: 1`).\n\n## 3. Common mistakes\n- **Expecting equal widths** from `flex-grow: 1` alone with different content.\n- **Setting grow on the container** - it's an item property.\n- **Huge grow numbers** - only the ratio matters (1:2 is the same as 10:20).\n\n## 4. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Build a top bar: fixed logo, a growing search input, and a fixed user avatar.\n2. Build a 3-column layout where the middle column is exactly twice as wide as each side column.\n3. Build a progress row where a label is fixed and the bar grows to fill the rest.\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<style>\n  body { font-family: system-ui; }\n  .bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 8px; background: #f1f5f9; border-radius: 10px; }\n  .bar input { flex-grow: 1; padding: 8px; }\n  .avatar { width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; background: #0f766e; }\n  .cols { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin: 12px 0; }\n  .cols div { flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0; padding: 12px; background: #e0e7ff; }\n  .cols .wide { flex-grow: 2; background: #c7d2fe; }\n  .progress { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }\n  .progress .track { flex-grow: 1; height: 10px; border-radius: 5px; background: linear-gradient(to right, #16a34a 0 70%, #e2e8f0 70%); }\n</style>\n<div class=\"bar\"><strong>Bargisy</strong><input placeholder=\"Search\"><span class=\"avatar\"></span></div>\n<div class=\"cols\"><div>Side</div><div class=\"wide\">Main (2x)</div><div>Side</div></div>\n<div class=\"progress\"><span>Q4 target</span><div class=\"track\"></div><span>70%</span></div>\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- flex-grow shares leftover space by ratio; default is 0.\n- Combine with flex-basis: 0 for exact proportions.\n- Classic use: a search input or main column that fills remaining space.\n",
