    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "summary": "Deep dive into modern Flexbox layout architecture: mastering the align-self property: overriding alignment on individual flex items.",
    "content": "# Lesson 56: The align-self Property: Overriding Alignment on Individual Flex Items\n\n`align-self` overrides the container's `align-items` for **one** item - letting a single element sit differently on the cross axis.\n\n## 1. Values\n`auto` (default - follow align-items), `flex-start`, `flex-end`, `center`, `baseline`, `stretch`.\n\n```css\n.container { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; }\n.special { align-self: flex-end; }\n```\n\n## 2. Related: order\n`order` changes the **visual position** of an item (default 0; lower numbers come first):\n```css\n.first { order: -1; }\n```\nLike `row-reverse`, it doesn't change keyboard/reading order - use it carefully.\n\n## 3. Worked examples\n### Example 1: One item breaks away\n```html\n<style>\n  .row { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; height: 140px; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 8px; font: 13px system-ui; }\n  .row div { background: #0ea5e9; color: white; padding: 10px; border-radius: 6px; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"row\">\n  <div>start</div>\n  <div style=\"align-self: center\">center</div>\n  <div style=\"align-self: flex-end\">end</div>\n  <div style=\"align-self: stretch\">stretch</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Example 2: Chat bubbles\n```html\n<style>\n  .chat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; width: 300px; padding: 10px; background: #e5ddd5; border-radius: 12px; font: 14px system-ui; }\n  .msg { max-width: 75%; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 12px; background: white; align-self: flex-start; }\n  .msg.me { align-self: flex-end; background: #dcf8c6; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"chat\">\n  <div class=\"msg\">Is the eye gel available?</div>\n  <div class=\"msg me\">Yes, 40 units in stock.</div>\n  <div class=\"msg\">Please reserve 10.</div>\n  <div class=\"msg me\">Done ✅</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Example 3: A \"Sale\" ribbon aligned to the top of a row\n```html\n<style>\n  .product { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 12px; width: 360px; font-family: system-ui; }\n  .product img { width: 70px; height: 70px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 8px; }\n  .product .tag { align-self: flex-start; margin-left: auto; background: #dc2626; color: white; font-size: 11px; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"product\">\n  <img src=\"https://picsum.photos/id/292/140/140\" alt=\"Vegetables\">\n  <div><strong>Healthy Box</strong><br>35 SAR</div>\n  <span class=\"tag\">SALE</span>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Example 4: Visual reordering with order\n```html\n<style>\n  .steps { display: flex; gap: 6px; font: 13px system-ui; }\n  .steps div { padding: 8px 12px; background: #e0e7ff; border-radius: 6px; }\n  .steps .featured { order: -1; background: #fde68a; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"steps\"><div>Basic</div><div>Standard</div><div class=\"featured\">Recommended (moved first)</div></div>\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> align-self is great for exceptions - a badge pinned to the top, a message on the right. If most items need the same alignment, set align-items on the container instead.\n\n## 4. Common mistakes\n- **Using align-self to move items along the main axis** - it only affects the cross axis (use margin auto for the main axis).\n- **`order` breaking keyboard order** for important content.\n- **Expecting align-self to work on non-flex/grid children.**\n\n## 5. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Build a support chat with agent messages on the left and customer messages on the right (align-self).\n2. In a row of three equal-height cards aligned to the top, make the middle \"Popular\" card centred and with no stretch.\n3. Use `order` to move a \"New\" card to the front visually.\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<style>\n  body { font-family: system-ui; }\n  .chat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; width: 300px; padding: 10px; background: #f1f5f9; border-radius: 12px; }\n  .chat p { margin: 0; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 10px; max-width: 75%; }\n  .agent { align-self: flex-start; background: white; }\n  .customer { align-self: flex-end; background: #2563eb; color: white; }\n  .cards { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; height: 180px; margin-top: 16px; }\n  .cards div { flex: 1; padding: 12px; background: #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; }\n  .cards .popular { align-self: center; background: #fde68a; }\n  .cards .new { order: -1; background: #bbf7d0; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"chat\"><p class=\"agent\">How can I help?</p><p class=\"customer\">Where is my order?</p><p class=\"agent\">It arrives today.</p></div>\n<div class=\"cards\"><div>Basic</div><div class=\"popular\">Popular</div><div>Premium</div><div class=\"new\">New</div></div>\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- align-self overrides align-items for a single item.\n- Perfect for chat bubbles, badges and exceptions.\n- `order` changes visual order only - use with care.\n",
