    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "summary": "Master modern two-dimensional CSS Grid layout: grid template areas: designing visual layouts with ascii art syntax.",
    "content": "# Lesson 71: Grid Template Areas: Designing Visual Layouts with ASCII Art Syntax\n\n`grid-template-areas` lets you **draw your layout with words**. Each string is a row, each word a cell - and items are placed by name. It's the most readable way to build page layouts.\n\n## 1. Syntax\n```css\n.page {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;\n  grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;\n  grid-template-areas:\n    \"header  header\"\n    \"sidebar main\"\n    \"footer  footer\";\n}\nheader { grid-area: header; }\naside  { grid-area: sidebar; }\nmain   { grid-area: main; }\nfooter { grid-area: footer; }\n```\nRules:\n- Every row string must have the **same number of cells**.\n- An area must be a **rectangle**.\n- Use a `.` for an empty cell.\n\n## 2. Worked examples\n### Example 1: Classic page layout\n```html\n<style>\n  .page { display: grid; gap: 8px; height: 300px; font: 14px system-ui;\n          grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr;\n          grid-template-rows: 56px 1fr 44px;\n          grid-template-areas: \"header header\" \"sidebar main\" \"footer footer\"; }\n  .page > * { padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px; }\n  .page header { grid-area: header; background: #0f172a; color: white; }\n  .page aside { grid-area: sidebar; background: #e0e7ff; }\n  .page main { grid-area: main; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; }\n  .page footer { grid-area: footer; background: #e2e8f0; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"page\"><header>Header</header><aside>Sidebar</aside><main>Main content</main><footer>Footer</footer></div>\n```\n\n### Example 2: Rearranging for mobile - just redraw\n```html\n<style>\n  .layout { display: grid; gap: 8px; font: 14px system-ui;\n            grid-template-areas: \"header\" \"main\" \"sidebar\" \"footer\"; }\n  .layout > * { padding: 12px; border-radius: 8px; }\n  .h { grid-area: header; background: #134e4a; color: white; }\n  .m { grid-area: main; background: #f0fdfa; min-height: 80px; }\n  .s { grid-area: sidebar; background: #fef9c3; }\n  .f { grid-area: footer; background: #e2e8f0; }\n  @media (min-width: 640px) {\n    .layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr 220px; grid-template-areas: \"header header\" \"main sidebar\" \"footer footer\"; }\n  }\n</style>\n<div class=\"layout\"><header class=\"h\">Header</header><main class=\"m\">Main</main><aside class=\"s\">Sidebar</aside><footer class=\"f\">Footer</footer></div>\n```\nThe HTML never changes - only the \"drawing\" does.\n\n### Example 3: Empty cells with dots\n```html\n<style>\n  .card { display: grid; gap: 8px; width: 320px; font: 13px system-ui;\n          grid-template-columns: 70px 1fr 60px;\n          grid-template-areas: \"avatar name  badge\" \"avatar role  .\" \"text   text  text\"; }\n  .card > * { background: #f1f5f9; padding: 6px; border-radius: 6px; }\n  .av { grid-area: avatar; background: #0f766e !important; color: white; display: grid; place-items: center; }\n  .nm { grid-area: name; font-weight: 700; }\n  .bd { grid-area: badge; background: #fde68a !important; text-align: center; }\n  .rl { grid-area: role; }\n  .tx { grid-area: text; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"av\">SA</div><div class=\"nm\">Sara Ali</div><div class=\"bd\">PRO</div>\n  <div class=\"rl\">Sales Rep - Makkah</div><div class=\"tx\">Top performer for Q3 with 118% achievement.</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Line the strings up in columns in your code (add spaces) - the CSS then literally looks like the layout.\n\n## 3. Common mistakes\n- **Rows with different cell counts** - the whole template becomes invalid.\n- **L-shaped areas** - areas must be rectangles.\n- **Typos between the template and `grid-area` names.**\n\n## 4. Hands-on Student Challenge\nBuild a dashboard with areas:\n```text\n\"header header header\"\n\"nav    stats  stats\"\n\"nav    chart  side\"\n\"footer footer footer\"\n```\nColumns: 180px 1fr 220px. Then add a media query below 700px that stacks everything in one column in this order: header, stats, chart, side, nav, footer.\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<style>\n  body { font-family: system-ui; }\n  .dash { display: grid; gap: 8px;\n          grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr 220px;\n          grid-template-rows: 56px 90px 200px 44px;\n          grid-template-areas:\n            \"header header header\"\n            \"nav    stats  stats\"\n            \"nav    chart  side\"\n            \"footer footer footer\"; }\n  .dash > * { padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px; background: #f1f5f9; }\n  .dash header { grid-area: header; background: #0f172a; color: white; }\n  .dash nav { grid-area: nav; background: #e0e7ff; }\n  .dash .stats { grid-area: stats; background: #dcfce7; }\n  .dash .chart { grid-area: chart; background: #dbeafe; }\n  .dash .side { grid-area: side; background: #fef3c7; }\n  .dash footer { grid-area: footer; }\n  @media (max-width: 700px) {\n    .dash { grid-template-columns: 1fr; grid-template-rows: auto;\n            grid-template-areas: \"header\" \"stats\" \"chart\" \"side\" \"nav\" \"footer\"; }\n  }\n</style>\n<div class=\"dash\">\n  <header>Header</header><nav>Navigation</nav><div class=\"stats\">KPI stats</div>\n  <div class=\"chart\">Chart</div><div class=\"side\">Activity</div><footer>Footer</footer>\n</div>\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- grid-template-areas draws the layout with named cells; grid-area assigns items.\n- Same number of cells per row, rectangular areas, `.` for empty cells.\n- Redraw the template in media queries to rearrange layouts without touching HTML.\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 71, Web Design, Advanced",
    "read_time": 5,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
    "status": "published",
    "views": 197,
    "cover_gradient": "linear-gradient(135deg, #075985, #38bdf8)",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-17 09:00:00"
