    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "summary": "Build adaptable, responsive interfaces across all screen sizes: fluid spacing & padding with clamp() and css math functions (calc, min, max).",
    "content": "# Lesson 81: Fluid Spacing & Padding with clamp() and CSS Math Functions (calc, min, max)\n\nCSS can do maths. `calc()`, `min()`, `max()` and `clamp()` let you mix units and create spacing that adapts to the screen - with fewer media queries.\n\n## 1. calc() - mix units\n```css\nwidth: calc(100% - 240px);           /* full width minus a sidebar */\nheight: calc(100vh - 64px);          /* screen height minus a header */\npadding: calc(1rem + 2vw);           /* fixed + fluid */\n```\nSpaces around `+` and `-` are **required**: `calc(100% - 20px)`.\n\n## 2. min() and max()\n```css\nwidth: min(90%, 1100px);    /* the SMALLER value: 90% on phones, max 1100px */\npadding: max(16px, 4vw);    /* the LARGER value: at least 16px */\n```\nTip: `min()` sets a **maximum**, `max()` sets a **minimum** - it sounds backwards, so think \"pick the smallest/largest\".\n\n## 3. clamp() for spacing\n```css\npadding: clamp(16px, 5vw, 64px);\ngap: clamp(8px, 2vw, 24px);\nmargin-block: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);\n```\n\n## 4. Worked examples\n### Example 1: A centred container in one line\n```html\n<style>\n  .container { width: min(92%, 960px); margin-inline: auto; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 16px; font-family: system-ui; box-sizing: border-box; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"container\">92% wide on small screens, never wider than 960px.</div>\n```\n\n### Example 2: Sidebar layout with calc()\n```html\n<style>\n  .wrap { display: flex; font: 13px system-ui; }\n  .side { width: 200px; background: #1e293b; color: white; padding: 10px; }\n  .main { width: calc(100% - 200px); background: #e0f2fe; padding: 10px; box-sizing: border-box; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"side\">200px</div><div class=\"main\">calc(100% - 200px)</div></div>\n```\n\n### Example 3: Fluid section spacing\n```html\n<style>\n  section { padding: clamp(16px, 6vw, 80px) clamp(16px, 4vw, 48px); font-family: system-ui; }\n  section:nth-child(odd) { background: #f8fafc; }\n  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(180px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: clamp(10px, 2.5vw, 28px); }\n  .grid div { background: #dbeafe; padding: 14px; border-radius: 10px; }\n</style>\n<section><h2>Fluid spacing</h2><p>Padding grows smoothly with the screen width.</p></section>\n<section><div class=\"grid\"><div>A</div><div>B</div><div>C</div><div>D</div></div></section>\n```\n\n### Example 4: Full-bleed inside a container\n```html\n<style>\n  .article { width: min(90%, 600px); margin: 0 auto; font-family: system-ui; }\n  .bleed { width: 100vw; margin-left: calc(50% - 50vw); background: #0f766e; color: white; padding: 20px; box-sizing: border-box; text-align: center; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"article\"><p>Normal article width.</p><div class=\"bleed\">This banner breaks out to the full screen width.</div><p>Back to normal.</p></div>\n```\n\n### Example 5: Using CSS variables in calculations\n```css\n:root { --space: 8px; --header: 64px; }\n.card { padding: calc(var(--space) * 3); }               /* 24px */\n.page { min-height: calc(100vh - var(--header)); }\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> `width: min(90%, 1100px); margin-inline: auto;` is the modern, one-line container - no media queries, no max-width + width pair.\n\n## 5. Common mistakes\n- **No spaces around operators**: `calc(100%-20px)` is invalid.\n- **Mixing up min() and max()** - remember they pick the smallest / largest.\n- **Dividing by a unit**: `calc(100px / 2px)` is invalid; divide by a plain number.\n\n## 6. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Create a container that is 94% wide up to a maximum of 1000px, centred, using min().\n2. Give sections vertical padding between 24px and 96px that scales with the viewport.\n3. Create a header 60px tall and a content area exactly the remaining screen height with calc().\n4. Make card padding at least 12px but growing to 3vw on large screens with max().\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body { margin: 0; font-family: system-ui; }\n  :root { --header: 60px; }\n  header { height: var(--header); background: #0f172a; color: white; display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 16px; }\n  .content { min-height: calc(100vh - var(--header)); padding-block: clamp(24px, 8vw, 96px); }\n  .container { width: min(94%, 1000px); margin-inline: auto; }\n  .card { padding: max(12px, 3vw); background: #f1f5f9; border-radius: 12px; }\n</style>\n<header>Bargisy</header>\n<main class=\"content\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"card\">Fluid card padding and spacing.</div></div></main>\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- calc() mixes units (% minus px, vh minus header).\n- min() caps a value, max() sets a floor, clamp() does both.\n- These functions create fluid spacing with fewer media queries.\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 81, Web Design, Advanced",
    "read_time": 4,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
    "status": "published",
    "views": 167,
    "cover_gradient": "linear-gradient(135deg, #075985, #38bdf8)",
