    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "summary": "Master advanced CSS motion, variables, and architecture: css transitions part 1: transition-property, duration, and delay.",
    "content": "# Lesson 89: CSS Transitions Part 1: transition-property, duration, and delay\n\n**Transitions** animate the change between two states - for example, from normal to hover - so changes feel smooth instead of instant.\n\n## 1. The properties\n\n| Property | Example | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `transition-property` | `background-color` | What to animate (`all` for everything) |\n| `transition-duration` | `0.3s` / `300ms` | How long |\n| `transition-timing-function` | `ease` | The speed curve (next lesson) |\n| `transition-delay` | `0.1s` | Wait before starting |\n\nShorthand: `transition: property duration timing-function delay;`\n```css\n.btn { transition: background-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease; }\n```\nThe transition goes on the **base** state, so it plays both when entering and leaving the hover.\n\n## 2. What can be animated?\nProperties with in-between values: colours, sizes, opacity, transform, box-shadow, border-radius, padding... **Not** `display` (it jumps) - use opacity/visibility.\n\n## 3. Worked examples\n### Example 1: Smooth button\n```html\n<style>\n  .btn { padding: 12px 22px; border: 0; border-radius: 10px; font: 600 15px system-ui; color: white; background: #2563eb; cursor: pointer;\n         transition: background-color .25s, transform .15s, box-shadow .25s; }\n  .btn:hover { background: #1d4ed8; box-shadow: 0 8px 18px rgba(37,99,235,.35); }\n  .btn:active { transform: scale(.96); }\n</style>\n<button class=\"btn\">Hover and click me</button>\n```\n\n### Example 2: Duration comparison\n```html\n<style>\n  .bar { height: 26px; width: 60px; margin: 6px 0; border-radius: 6px; background: #0ea5e9; color: white; font: 12px system-ui; padding: 4px 8px; box-sizing: border-box; }\n  .area:hover .bar { width: 100%; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"area\" style=\"border:1px dashed #94a3b8;padding:8px\">\n  <p style=\"font:600 13px system-ui;margin:0\">Hover this box:</p>\n  <div class=\"bar\" style=\"transition: width .1s\">0.1s</div>\n  <div class=\"bar\" style=\"transition: width .3s\">0.3s</div>\n  <div class=\"bar\" style=\"transition: width 1s\">1s</div>\n  <div class=\"bar\" style=\"transition: width .5s .5s\">0.5s delay</div>\n</div>\n```\nUI transitions usually feel best between **150ms and 300ms**.\n\n### Example 3: Staggered delays\n```html\n<style>\n  .menu { font-family: system-ui; }\n  .menu li { opacity: .3; transform: translateX(-10px); transition: opacity .3s, transform .3s; list-style: none; padding: 4px 0; }\n  .menu:hover li { opacity: 1; transform: none; }\n  .menu li:nth-child(2) { transition-delay: .08s; }\n  .menu li:nth-child(3) { transition-delay: .16s; }\n  .menu li:nth-child(4) { transition-delay: .24s; }\n</style>\n<ul class=\"menu\" style=\"border:1px dashed #94a3b8;padding:10px;width:200px\"><li>Dashboard</li><li>Reports</li><li>Customers</li><li>Settings</li></ul>\n```\n\n### Example 4: Fade in/out with visibility\n```html\n<style>\n  .tip { opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; transition: opacity .2s, visibility .2s; background: #0f172a; color: white; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 6px; font: 13px system-ui; display: inline-block; }\n  .wrap:hover .tip { opacity: 1; visibility: visible; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"wrap\" style=\"font-family:system-ui\">Hover for help ⓘ <span class=\"tip\">Totals include VAT</span></div>\n```\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Avoid `transition: all` - it animates properties you didn't intend (and can hurt performance). List the specific properties.\n\n## 4. Common mistakes\n- **Putting the transition only on `:hover`** - it animates in but snaps back out.\n- **Transitioning `display`** - doesn't work.\n- **Durations that are too long** - the interface feels slow.\n\n## 5. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Create a card whose border colour and shadow change smoothly on hover (250ms).\n2. Create a link whose underline grows from 0 to full width on hover using a pseudo-element and a width transition.\n3. Create an input whose border colour transitions when focused.\n\n:::solution\n```html\n<style>\n  body { font-family: system-ui; }\n  .card { width: 240px; padding: 16px; border: 2px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 12px; transition: border-color .25s, box-shadow .25s; }\n  .card:hover { border-color: #0f766e; box-shadow: 0 10px 22px rgba(15,118,110,.18); }\n  .link { position: relative; color: #1d4ed8; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin: 16px 0; }\n  .link::after { content: \"\"; position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: -3px; height: 2px; width: 0; background: currentColor; transition: width .25s ease; }\n  .link:hover::after { width: 100%; }\n  .field { padding: 10px; border: 2px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; outline: none; transition: border-color .2s, box-shadow .2s; }\n  .field:focus { border-color: #2563eb; box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(37,99,235,.2); }\n</style>\n<div class=\"card\">Hover card</div>\n<a class=\"link\" href=\"#\">Animated underline</a><br>\n<input class=\"field\" placeholder=\"Focus me\">\n```\n:::\n\n## Key takeaways\n- transition: property duration timing delay - placed on the base state.\n- Animate colours, opacity, transform, shadows; not display.\n- Keep UI transitions around 150-300ms and list specific properties.\n",
    "tags": "CSS, Front-End, Lesson 89, Web Design, Advanced",
    "read_time": 5,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
